notation	applies to	rule	rationale
python	package (folder)	lowercase; spaces and hyphens as underscores; a module named with ›, its name after the last ›	PEP8 Package and Module Names; Files: a module written with › in the folder of its parent
python	function	lowercase; spaces and hyphens as underscores; a keyword, then _	PEP8 Function and Variable Names; PEP8 Function and Method Arguments: a trailing underscore for a name that clashes with a reserved keyword
python	parameter	as the Parameter column writes it	PEP8 Function and Variable Names
python	exception	the words, split at each space and hyphen, each capitalized, joined, then Error	PEP8 Exception Names; Class Names
python	test class	Test, then the module, its name after the last ›, as an exception's words without Error	PY-UNITTEST Basic example; PEP8 Class Names
python	test method	test_, then the requirement's identifier, hyphens and full stops as underscores	PY-UNITTEST: methods whose names start with test
python	detail	_, then the name as PEP8 writes its kind	PEP8 Public and Internal Interfaces
python	value	the requirement's identifier, then the operation, each word lowercase, spaces, hyphens and full stops as underscores, joined by _	PEP8 Function and Variable Names; Operation uses: a use is keyed by its requirement and operation, so each use's value has one name in its body
javascript	folder and file	lowercase; spaces as hyphens; a module named with ›, its name after the last ›	NPM-PACKAGE-JSON: a name lowercase and URL-safe; Files: a module written with › in the folder of its parent
javascript	function	the words, split at each space, hyphen and underscore: the first lowercase, each later one capitalized, joined; a ReservedWord, then _, its local name only, the export keeping the access program's name (3-statements, ExportDeclaration)	ECMA-262: the built-in functions' names, as parseInt and getOwnPropertyNames; ECMA-262 12.7.2: a ReservedWord is not an Identifier; ECMA-262 16.2.3: the export under its own name
javascript	parameter	as a function	ECMA-262: as the built-ins' parameters
javascript	error	each word capitalized, joined, then Error	ECMA-262: the NativeError constructors, as TypeError and RangeError
javascript	detail	as a function, and not exported	ECMA-262 16.2.3 Exports: a binding a module does not export is reached by none other
javascript	value	the requirement's identifier, then the operation, as a function, a full stop also splitting words	ECMA-262 14.3.1: a const declaration binds a name once in its block; Operation uses: a use is keyed by its requirement and operation
7-relations
relation	lands in	rationale
Scope	—	QAFRAME Good Practice 2: informative; no code
Clause	—	QAFRAME Requirement 1: the conformance clause; normative, read, no code
Clause citations	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
References	—	RFC7322 4.8.6: the references section; no code
Axes	—	ISO25010: higher-level requirements; traced, no code
Types	3-statements, 4-expressions	PEP484: a type is an annotation; JavaScript has none in canon's templates; Written: how a conformance case writes a value of the type, read by the runner from its cases, no code of its own
Enumerations	—	PARNAS1985 MODULE DESCRIPTION: values a body uses are its secondary secret
Modules	3-statements, 5-texts	PEP257 and GNU 5.2: the module docstring says what the file is for; PARNAS1985: a module is described by its secret; PARNAS1979 D: a parent imports each of its parts
Values	—	PARNAS1985 B:3.4: read by name at run time from values.mtsv
Value citations	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
Components	2-modules, 3-statements, 5-texts	PYPA-ENTRY-POINTS and NPM-PACKAGE-JSON: each started component is a [project.scripts] entry and a bin entry
Files	1-folders, 2-modules	canon 1-structure: FOLDER and MODULE; PARNAS1985: containment is a tree
Relations	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	PARNAS1985: the relations a body reads and writes are its secondary secret, no code of their own; a relation whose records its book holds as a sheet, other than the specification's own sheets, is data the bodies use, compiled as Enumerations are into each module whose requirements name it (PARNAS1985 MODULE DESCRIPTION), a detail of that module, handed by no Parameters row
Domains	—	PARNAS1985: as Relations
Signatures	3-statements, 4-expressions	PEP484 Callable: a callable type's arguments and return
Access programs	3-statements, 5-texts	PARNAS1985 DESIGN PRINCIPLE: a module is reached only through its access programs
Parameters	4-expressions, 5-texts	PEP484 and ECMA-262: a parameter
Parameter relations	—	PARNAS1985: the relations a parameter carries are its body's secondary secret; the annotation is the relations Type's; traced, no code
Results	4-expressions	PEP484: the return annotation; JavaScript has none in canon's templates
Result relations	—	PARNAS1985: as Parameter relations; traced, no code
Errors	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	PEP8 Exception Names and ECMA-262: an error class in each module that raises it, as its interface states it (PARNAS1985); void-os.3: a called error no requirement ends passes up by its name
Ended errors	3-statements	void-os.3: an error a requirement ends is a handler that carries that requirement out; one ruled out is no statement
Compositions	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	PARNAS1979 D: a part reaches another module only through what its parent hands it
Connectors	—	FIELDING2000 1.2.2: architecture; traced, no code
Requirements	2-modules, 3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	QAFRAME Good Practice 12: a test assertion per requirement
Operations	3-statements, 4-expressions	QAFRAME Good Practice 10, the register's rule for an operation a requirement names: a primitive is its Bindings Code; a grammar is written rule by rule as statements; a composite as its Operation steps
Operation inputs	3-statements	Bindings Code: each Input the placeholder between {{ and }} the value handed at its Position fills; its Type traced, no annotation, the Code having none
Bindings	3-statements	Bindings Code: one line in the notation's grammar, the statements it parses to, and the imports of the names it reads (PY-IMPORT; NODE-PACKAGES)
Operation steps	3-statements	each step a statement of the composite operation's body, in Position order
Control words	3-statements	8-control words: each word the statement its notation's grammar gives it
Terms	—	QAFRAME Good Practice 10: definitions; traced, no code
Value uses	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
Operation uses	4-expressions	PARNAS1985: each use is a call in the body of the access program that carries the requirement out
Access program uses	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	PARNAS1985 DESIGN PRINCIPLE: each use is a call of another module's access program; one of a part's of the same name and Parameters gives it as the node's own (RESTRICTED AND HIDDEN MODULES)
Citations	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
Spec relations	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
Axis rules	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: traced, no code
Requirement files	—	NPR-7150-2D 3.12: a repository file a requirement states, checked by its cases; traced, no code
harness members	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	Relations: compiled into hooks (hooks.2), hook output (hook-output.1) and zoom (zoom.5), a detail of each; Tag, Section and First block traced, no code
harness variables	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	Relations: compiled into hooks (hooks.2), a detail; Tag, Section and First block traced, no code
context members	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	Relations: compiled into hook output (hooks.4, hook-output.1), a detail; Tag, Section and First block traced, no code
answer members	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	Relations: compiled into hook output (hook-output.7), a detail; Tag, Section and First block traced, no code
tool arguments	3-statements, 4-expressions, 5-texts	Relations: compiled into server (server.3, server.6), a detail
